                ## 2. Detailed Kali Linux Installation Guide## Pre-requisites & Preparation

* Download: Secure the official ISO image only from the verified [Kali Linux Website](https://www.kali.org/).
* Deployment Choice: You can install Kali as a primary OS (bare metal), dual-boot alongside Windows, or run it isolated inside a virtual machine (VirtualBox or VMware).

## Step-by-Step Installation Process

   1. Booting the Medium: Insert your bootable USB or mount the ISO in your virtual machine. Select Graphical Install from the boot menu.
   2. Localization: Choose your preferred language, geographic location, and keyboard layout (e.g., English, United States, American English).
   3. Network Configuration:
   * The installer automatically attempts to configure network settings via DHCP.
      * Enter a Hostname (the name identifying your system on the network, e.g., kali-box).
      * Enter a Domain name (leave blank if you are setting this up in a home/basic lab environment).
   4. User Accounts: Set up a non-root administrative user account. Provide a full name, username, and a strong password.
   5. Disk Partitioning:
   * For beginners/virtual machines: Select Guided - use entire disk.
      * Choose the target hard drive.
      * Select All files in one partition (recommended for new users).
      * Confirm changes by selecting Finish partitioning and write changes to disk.
   6. Package Selection: Select the desktop environment (XFCE is the default and highly recommended for performance) and the collection of tools you wish to install (Top 10, default, or large).
   7. GRUB Bootloader: When prompted to install the GRUB bootloader to your primary drive, select Yes and choose your main storage device (e.g., /dev/sda).
   8. Finalize: Once completed, remove your installation media and click Continue to reboot into your new system.

